  31:../src/register.c ****  * For each register, this includes initial (default) values optional read and write
  32:../src/register.c ****  * callbacks are used to query hardware and for enforcing permissions. For example, a write callbac
  33:../src/register.c ****  * simply returning an error value is used to make a register read only. When a callback is non-zer
  34:../src/register.c ****  * after initialization, it is prioritized over SRAM.
